---
description: Cross-tool work log — append after finishing non-trivial work
alwaysApply: true
---

This project is also worked on from Claude Code, which cannot see Cursor's
session history or memory. `dev-notes/agent-log.md` is the shared bridge
between the two.

After finishing a non-trivial, non-obvious piece of work in this repo
(a real bug fix, a design decision with a non-obvious reason, a gotcha
specific to this codebase, a dead end that shouldn't be retried), append an
entry to `dev-notes/agent-log.md` following the format documented at the top
of that file: a dated `## YYYY-MM-DD — Cursor — <summary>` heading followed
by a few sentences on what changed, why, and anything surprising (especially
root causes, not just symptoms). Reference specific files/functions.

Don't log routine or self-explanatory edits — only what a future session
(in either tool) would otherwise have to rediscover from scratch.
